Description: A 3D render keeps the source's depth, or says it writes fewer bits
 In a 3D project a 3D preset that names no pixel format writes the depth of the
 deepest video clip up to its codec's: H.264 10 bits (High 10), H.265 12 (Main
 12, as libx265 writes it), FFV1 16, through MLT's RGBA64 frame above 10 bits.
 When a render writes fewer bits than the deepest clip, the person is told
 before it runs, in the render dialog and on the command line, and the render
 goes ahead. A 3D Matroska-FFV1 (lossless) preset is added.
